          {
            "section_type": "example_question",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Write <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 0.\\overline{23}]</span> as geometric series.</p>",
            "readable_text": "Write [MATH: 0.\\overline{23}] as geometric series.",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>EXPLANATION</p>",
            "readable_text": "EXPLANATION",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "example_explanation",
            "normalized_html": "<p>The given repeating decimal can be written as \n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: 0.\\overline{23} = 0.23 + 0.002\\,3 + 0.000\\,023 + \\dots]</span>\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: 0.\\overline{23} = \\dfrac{23}{100} + \\dfrac{23}{10\\,000} + \\dfrac{23}{1\\,000\\,000}+\\dots]</span>\nwhere the first term is <span class=\"math\">[MATH: a_1 = \\dfrac{23}{100}]</span> and the common ratio is <span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\dfrac{1}{100}.]</span> Therefore,\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: 0.23^(\u2015)|= \u2211_(n = 1)^(\u221e)a_{1}r^{n \u2212 1}; = \u2211_(n = 1)^(\u221e)(23)/(100) \u22c5 ((1)/(100))^{n \u2212 1}; = \u2211_(n = 1)^(\u221e)23 \u22c5 (1)/(100) \u22c5 ((1)/(100))^{n \u2212 1}; = \u2211_(n = 1)^(\u221e)23 \u22c5 (1)/(100) \u22c5 ((1)/(100))^{n} \u22c5 ((1)/(100))^{\u2212 1}; = \u2211_(n = 1)^(\u221e)23((1)/(100))^{n}.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "The given repeating decimal can be written as\n[MATH: 0.\\overline{23} = 0.23 + 0.002\\,3 + 0.000\\,023 + \\dots]\n[MATH: 0.\\overline{23} = \\dfrac{23}{100} + \\dfrac{23}{10\\,000} + \\dfrac{23}{1\\,000\\,000}+\\dots]\nwhere the first term is [MATH: a_1 = \\dfrac{23}{100}] and the common ratio is [MATH: \\dfrac{1}{100}.] Therefore,\n[MATH: 0.23^(\u2015)|= \u2211_(n = 1)^(\u221e)a_{1}r^{n \u2212 1}; = \u2211_(n = 1)^(\u221e)(23)/(100) \u22c5 ((1)/(100))^{n \u2212 1}; = \u2211_(n = 1)^(\u221e)23 \u22c5 (1)/(100) \u22c5 ((1)/(100))^{n \u2212 1}; = \u2211_(n = 1)^(\u221e)23 \u22c5 (1)/(100) \u22c5 ((1)/(100))^{n} \u22c5 ((1)/(100))^{\u2212 1}; = \u2211_(n = 1)^(\u221e)23((1)/(100))^{n}.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [],
